# Config constants

Hardcoded values that can be reused belong in [`src/config.ts`](src/config.ts). Do not scatter duplicates across the codebase.

## Put in config

- User-facing messages (asks, notes, status text, errors)
- URLs, hosts, API origins, path prefixes
- Timeouts, limits, budgets, intervals, viewport sizes
- Feature thresholds (stall, strategy, sparse screenshot, recent history)

## Keep local

- One-off test fixtures
- Truly unique one-line prompt scaffolding that is not reused
- Domain regexes that encode policy logic (unless shared)

## How

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — magic string in the loop
this.ask("I stopped after many actions without reaching the end.", "verify")

// ✅ GOOD — shared constant
import { BUDGET_STOP_QUESTION } from "../config.js"
this.ask(BUDGET_STOP_QUESTION, "verify")
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
setInterval(tick, 30_000)

// ✅ GOOD
import { GRACE_POLL_MS } from "../config.js"
setInterval(tick, GRACE_POLL_MS)
```

When adding a new shared value: export it from `src/config.ts`, import it where used, and prefer an existing name over inventing a second constant for the same meaning.
